WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.900
Kokonotsu... You were right.
It seems my idea was indeed mistaken.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.110
Yes?

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.780
Do you know what happens to cakes
when you fail to sell them regularly?

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.440
They went bad, huh?

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.280
Yes... It was quite sad to see.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.780
The Special Sweets corner...!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.280
"Whole Cakes - 3,500 yen each (plus tax)"

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.620
So I switched over to a made-to-order system.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.540
What?

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.710
I guess even in a remote town
like this, there is a demand!

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.960
They're selling quite well!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.040
O-Okay...

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:33.800
Customers can order them at the store,
on the phone, or via the Internets, so...!

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.550
Thanks for coming!

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.010
The Internets, huh?

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.770
Let's see... This one goes...

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.800
Welcome back, Manager.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.560
The Internets... The Nets...

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.650
The Inter... The Inter...

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.620
The Internets, huh?

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:54.500
Ah!

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.660
The Internets!

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.410
Ah!

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.290
Oh? Did you just hide something?

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.920
Um... I was writing in my diary.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.420
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:14.300
Anyway, listen! We'll use
Internets shopping, too!

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.850
Um... Are you going to 
buy manga or something?

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:26.980
My honey!

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:30.110
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling,
when I take a bite

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.980
That sugar feeling, sugar 
feeling flows into me

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:40.910
The crackling sparkle is 
giving me a sugar rush

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:46.250
I'm stuffed... I can't...
but I'm hungry for more!

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:49.460
A scent drifts into the air...

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:52.630
Could it be you?

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:58.800
With those footsteps that sound like
a colorful and full candy box shaking

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:08.690
I feel like I can reach that cotton
candy in the sky, but it's no good

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:14.900
Don't melt away! Don't disappear!
I want to tell you my feelings!

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.650
You're hungry?

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.190
My honey!

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.860
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:22.620
The first bite was full of mystery

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.240
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:29.000
The second bite got me hopelessly addicted

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.500
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.340
The more I chew, the deeper the flavor

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.960
That sugar feeling, sugar feeling

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:42.850
Before I knew it, I was
completely crazy about you

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:47.850
I'm stuffed... I can't...
but I'm hungry for more!

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.480
I see...

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.940
So you wanna sell dagashi
and toys on the Internet, huh?

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.650
I suppose pretty much every business
should be online these days.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.780
Right?! So in order to do that, I'd like to
start by creating a website for our shop!

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.500
So, as a first step, I created a draft site.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:10.250
What, already?!

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:15.000
"Website for Shikada Dagashi"
"Content / Contact us"

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.000
A-Awesome... You're great at the Internets!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.170
Hypertext Markup Language.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.010
I learned it in gloomy compulsory education.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:23.050
So this is the famous HTML.

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.760
The site's pretty boring right now, so...

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.510
"Content"

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.510
Whoa!

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:31.310
That sparkling thing is following
the mouse as it moves around...

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.310
That's so nostalgic!

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:34.770
This is...

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.780
...JavaScript!

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.780
So this is the famous JavaScript!

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.530
This is incredible... You can do
anything with computers!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.870
This is civilization!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.460
Shall we try putting in something?
Let's see, for example...

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.920
What would be our selling point?

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.530
Selling point... Selling point... Err...

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.050
W-We sell dagashi!

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:09.310
Yes, we do.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.310
"We sell dagashi"

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.650
Too much...! It's too much!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:21.070
The text! The text is
endlessly scrolling sideways!

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.070
"Website for Shikada Dagashi"
"Content / Contact us"
"We sell dagashi"

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.070
And we do this and...

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.320
"We sell dagashi"

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:32.000
They're... They're shining like crazy!

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.830
It's pushing hard that we sell dagashi
even though it's obvious we do!

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.090
Yeah, we run a dagashi shop!
It even says Shikada Dagashi!

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.550
I'm really starting to have fun.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.340
Same here!

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.540
Oh, yeah...

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.850
"Standby"

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.850
Yeah. Like that.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:54.380
Say cheese!

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.610
So we import this picture
and put it on the top page.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.940
"We sell dagashi"

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:01.610
"I'm the (temporary) manager"

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:06.160
Wh-Why?!

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.410
I made sure to put a 
black bar over your eyes.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.870
And then, if I just do this...

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:14.620
"I'm the (temporary) manager"

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.120
Too many! Too many of me!

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:19.880
Oh, yeah. Since we're doing this,
I might as well put mine up, too.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.820
Adding a black bar is a pain,
so I'll use my hand.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.220
And, we'll say that we can deliver dagashi.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.260
What else should we put in?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:32.140
Something like the nostalgic
appeal of dagashi shops...

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.600
Maybe we should try pushing that angle?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.890
Good idea! That lazy-day feeling, huh?

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.650
Let's see... Okay!

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:39.770
"Shikada' employee"
"Hajime"
"(20 years old)"

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.610
"We offer simple pleasures..."

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.780
"Shikada' employee"
"Hajime"
"(20 years old) "We offer simple pleasures..."

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.640
Well... Err...

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.070
Yeah...

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:50.780
But we're just trying
to advertise the shop, so...

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:51.780
Yeah.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.950
Ah! Also, we sell toys, too!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.290
Oh, yeah!

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.240
We have to put that... in.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.290
"We've got toys, too..."

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.710
And...

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.420
"We've got toys, too... / We deliver"

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.550
...we also put that we deliver dagashi.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.880
"We've got toys, too... / We deliver"
"We offer simple pleasures..."

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:09.550
"We've got toys, too... / We deliver"
"We offer simple pleasures..."
"Shikada' employee" "Hajime" "(20 years old)"

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.720
We went too far, didn't we?

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.350
We did.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.890
We completely got carried away.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.780
Yeah.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.100
I'll start over.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.120
Yeah.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.360
And so, and so...

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.150
Well then... I think what we ordered
should arrive in the morning, so...

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.660
Hm? You ordered something?

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:34.160
What?

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.960
It's the one you said
you'd take care of yourself.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.670
Hm...? Did you forget by any chance?

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:46.170
O-Of course not! Just kidding!
I was just kidding!

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:47.670
Of course it'll arrive today!

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:50.630
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.300
Oh, okay...

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.430
Y-Yes! See you later!

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.560
I forgot about it!

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.810
Shoot! I wonder if they'll
deliver it today if I order it now...

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.810
Err... That one, right...? Super Ball.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:03.650
"Super Ball / Win Big!"

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:07.570
Well, it's not like it 
sells all the time, so...

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.230
So that was the end!

00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:10.060
Wow...!

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:11.570
W-Welcome.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:15.870
What?! They don't have
even a single Super Ball!

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.580
"Super Ball / Win Big!"

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.870
You're right! Seriously?! They're useless!

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:23.160
I'm sorry! We're just out of them right now.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.590
What? I wanted to win a big one
first thing in the morning today!

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.590
Why'd you even bother reopening the shop?!

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.200
How pathetic.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.640
You're gonna go out of 
business soon like this.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.060
Let's go to the convenience store.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.850
"Go out of business"

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:41.140
This isn't good... If I don't do anything,
they'll stop coming here.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:44.230
Think... Think, Hajime!

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:47.280
Hold on a sec, boys!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.860
A Huge Super Ball!

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.860
Don't you want a Super Ball
that's just the size you want?

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.370
What?

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:59.120
"Salt"
"Laundry Starch"

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:57.950
What's this?

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.410
Salt, water, laundry starch, and...

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.960
I didn't mean that. Where 
are the Super Balls?

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:03.870
He's right!

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.670
You sure are impatient.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.920
You'll never become an adult like that.

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:14.340
First, add salt to a glass of water.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:17.280
Then, stir well so that the salt dissolves.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.720
Next, add the laundry starch to it.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:24.650
Let's see... You, the impatient one!

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:26.770
What's your favorite color?

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.820
I-I'm not impatient!

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.150
He is impatient, isn't he...

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.150
Blue.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:33.650
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:37.660
Then I'll use peacock blue,
my favorite color, for you.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.910
Squeeze just a little bit into the glass.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:44.770
And then stir, stir, and stir some more...

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.290
...and voila, you have a Super Ball!

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:50.100
Th-That's gross!

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.550
That's not a ball!

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.950
Now, now...

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.930
You really are an impatient one.
You won't be a hit with the ladies like that.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:09:00.680
Now, roll it around and around some more...

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.520
When some water comes out, just wipe it up...
I guess my clothes will do.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:05.690
And roll it some more...

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:06.810
Okay!

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:10.690
Here you go! It's a Super Ball just for you!

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:14.190
Just... for me...

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.050
Just for me!

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:21.000
Whoa! You're an alchemist, lady!

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.450
Make one for me, too!

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.500
--M-Me, too!
--Cool!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.710
Okay! It'll be thirty-yen!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.340
Shoot! We're late for school!

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:36.300
I somehow pulled through,
but what am I gonna do...?

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:39.470
I still haven't done anything
about the order I forgot to place...

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.470
I guess I'll make them.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:45.640
I kept making Super Balls...

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.970
...out of my firm desire to keep
Kokonotsu from finding out about it.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.480
"Salt"

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:53.570
The time I spent on it 
was strangely fulfilling.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:58.070
I wonder how long it's been
since I worked on something...

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:01.410
...with such clear 
determination... Hajime Owari.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.660
F... Finished!

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.170
I made so many of them.
This should be enough. Yep!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:11.840
Ah... All that hard work has made me hungry.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.550
I think I'll go eat something.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:22.050
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:22.050
Ah!

00:10:22.390 --> 00:10:24.200
And my brother was like...

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:25.560
What?

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:32.110
Err... What's this?

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.250
W... Welcome back.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:37.990
"Internets, Super Ball, and..."

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.280
Yeah.

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:51.130
On that summer day,
we ate popsicles under the sun

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:54.380
I still have the winning stick you gave me

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.380
'cause I'm worried that 
if I take it to the shop

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.670
even the memory will melt 
away like a popsicle

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.840
I'm such a fool to think that way, aren't I?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.970
As the seasons pass, you get even taller

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.140
The dream that was vague
has gotten a bit clearer

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.810
When I felt kind of worried 
and held you tight

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:13.610
you, with your eyes as sweet
as honey, smiled at me

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.780
Festivals, fireworks, that hot summer

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:19.950
Christmas, Valentine's, the freezing winter

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:24.990
Let's spend the next season together, too

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.290
"It's a promise, okay?"

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:32.370
Adolescence? Who cares about it?
I don't care about forever, either

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:39.170
Beyond the seasons gone by lies the future

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:45.180
I wonder if this pain will go away someday

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:55.310
That's what I was thinking as we ate the same
candy under the same sky on our way home

00:11:55.310 --> 00:12:01.950
I'm strange, aren't I? To feel
like it's a little bittersweet

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time:
'Monjiro Squid, Manga Manuscript, and...'"

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.580
Next time. "Monjiro Squid,
Manga Manuscript, and..."

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:14.650
Manager! Are you telling the truth?!
